module alnd-criminal-local-rules.local-rules

// The Northern District's Local Rules state no criminal period. The
// procedures for assigning criminal matters to magistrate judges,
// "including dates conferred or imposed on United States Magistrate Judges
// by statute or by the Federal Rules of Criminal Procedure", are in the
// court's General and Standing Orders (LR 72.1(c)); those orders are not
// vendored, so any district criminal practice they set is a hole. The
// rules that reach every case also reach a criminal one: electronic filing
// and service under the court's General Order and the criminal
// administrative procedures (LR 5.5, 5.6), juror interrogation (LR 47.1),
// attorneys (LR 83.1) and broadcasting (LR 83.2); none states a criminal
// period. Every criminal period (presentment, the preliminary hearing,
// Rule 12 motions, Rule 16 discovery, Rules 29, 33 and 35, the presentence
// report, the Speedy Trial Act and FRAP 4(b)) is lit/frcrimp's. The
// earlier outline's FRCrimP flow and its decisions belong to lit/frcrimp
// and are removed here: no reporter text is vendored.
